Their licence texts are collected in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md (generated from Cargo.lock by
scripts/third_party_licenses.py), which the Docker image ships in /opt/rawatta/.


Docker image
------------
The image built from docker/Dockerfile starts from NVIDIA's nvidia/cuda runtime image (CUDA
runtime, NVRTC, cuBLASLt), which is governed by the NVIDIA Deep Learning Container License
(/NGC-DL-CONTAINER-LICENSE in the image). The Ubuntu packages it installs (ffmpeg, Python, numpy,
curl, ...) keep their own licences (/usr/share/doc/*/copyright in the image).

ffmpeg in the image is Ubuntu 24.04's build, licensed GPL-2.0-or-later as built by Ubuntu. Its
corresponding source is Ubuntu's ffmpeg source package at the version installed in the image
(`dpkg-query -W ffmpeg` inside it; 7:6.1.1-3ubuntu5 when this was written): get it with
`apt-get source ffmpeg=<version>` on Ubuntu 24.04 or from
https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/ffmpeg.


Data
----
No dataset is redistributed. eval/data/ downloads each dataset from its source; eval/DATASETS.md
lists their licences, several of which are noncommercial. eval/manifests/ holds frame indices and
SHA-256 sums only. The example photos (examples/*/) are not stored in the repository; each
scene's SOURCE.md records its source and licence (Buddha Dataset: CC BY 4.0, Gasparini, Castan
and Lanthony, AliceVision; Korno climbing rock: CC0 1.0, Zbytovsky, Wikimedia Commons).
